        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Vimscript is an intentional feature, it's never going away. Your request makes no sense. Vimscript is a DSL that is very useful for the `:` cmdline. \n\nIf you're asking specifically about the baggage in the runtime files, well, that's harmless, it is never executed unless you actually use it. And for example we will drop netrw, which is the biggest remaining builtin vimscript plugin.",
